{"id":"u-be48ce3b-4986-4ca6-aa18-20be859bf4dd","src":"community","title":"Hybrid Hypertrophy 5","author":"Adam R.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ll18wC-hybrid-hypertrophy-5","desc":"Hybrid Hypertrophy 5 was built because I struggled to find an existing program that fit the way I actually wanted to train. Some programs had great arm work but were missing movements I enjoyed. Others had good exercise selection but felt too restrictive, repetitive, or didn’t give enough attention to the muscle groups I wanted to prioritize.\n\nInstead of continuing to jump between programs, I combined the parts that worked best for me into one structured 16-week plan.\nThe program focuses on hypertrophy with extra attention to arms, chest and shoulders, while still providing complete lower-body and back training. It uses familiar exercises long enough to actually improve at them, but introduces planned changes throughout the program so training doesn’t become stale.\n\nThe 16 weeks progress through Foundation, Build, Overload, Specialization and Reset phases, with a dedicated recovery cardio day built into each week.\n\nThe goal is simple: build muscle, progressively improve performance, enjoy the workouts, and have a program that feels sustainable enough to actually finish.","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-20T01:31:19.280Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Arm Specialization","Lower Body Foundation","Torso Development","Recovery Cardio","Delt Specialization"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Hammer Curl (Rope)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Tricep E